{"type":"message","id":"65a06fd7","parentId":"9ec758cb","timestamp":"2026-05-26T23:17:00.848Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is questioning why the stop loss triggered at only -0.634 USDT when it should be 2% = 4 USDT. Let me think about this.\n\nSOUL.md says:\n- Single position margin: 20 USDT (20%)\n- Leverage: 10x\n- Single nominal value: 200 USDT\n- Stop loss guarantee: ≤ -3%\n\nThe user expects stop loss at 2% of 200 USDT = 4 USDT, but it triggered at -0.634 USDT.\n\nLet me look at the actual DOT trade:\n- Entry: SHORT at $1.262\n- Stop loss was set at: $1.27 (as seen in the log: \"📌 DOTUSDT 止损 Algo 单已提交：1.27\")\n- Quantity: 158.5 DOT\n- Nominal value: 158.5 * 1.262 = ~$200 USDT\n\nFor a SHORT position:\n- If price goes UP to $1.27, loss = ($1.27 - $1.262) * 158.5 = $0.008 * 158.5 = $1.268\n\nBut the user saw -0.634 USDT. That's odd. Unless the stop loss triggered at a different price than $1.27, or the position was partially closed, or the actual fill price was different.\n\nWait, let me recalculate differently. The user says -0.634. Let me see what price change would give that:\n-0.634 / 158.5 = -0.004 = 0.4 cents loss per DOT\n\nSo if entry was $1.262, the close must have been around $1.266. That's 0.4 cents, not 0.8 cents (which would be the $1.27 stop loss).\n\nActually wait - the SL was an algo order at $1.27. But maybe the position was actually closed by a different mechanism - perhaps a trailing stop or the monitor's SL logic kicked in at a different price?\n\nLet me look at the actual BUY execution price from the logs. The user says history shows \"0:13分卖出3:32分买入\" - but at 03:32 the monitor log shows it was trying to OPEN a new short, not close. So maybe the close happened at a different time.\n\nLet me also consider: the monitor has a \"三档移动止盈止损\" logic. Maybe DOT was stopped out earlier than $1.27 due to some dynamic stop loss calculation.\n\nActually, looking at SOUL.md again:\n```\n止损 = max(支撑位×0.995, 价格×(1-ATR×分层倍数), 24h低点×0.98)\n保底: 止损≤-3%\n```\n\nSo the stop loss is calculated dynamically, not fixed at 2%. The 2% is the \"第1档\" of take profit moving stop, not the stop loss.\n\nThe SL at $1.27 was the initial stop loss order. But maybe the dynamic stop calculation was different, or maybe the algo order triggered at a different fill price.\n\nLet me search for the DOT close in the logs more carefully.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_j78GSnRDBWCe9ryTkhts4446","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep 'DOT' /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | grep -E '平仓|止损触发|SL.*触发|止盈|close|BUY|algo.*filled|已平' | head -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_NjLwraWiJ0FJQP8QUS9k7675","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep 'DOT' /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | grep -E '2026-05-27 0[1-3]:' | grep -v '价格已从\\|K 线\\|Ticker\\|klines\\|ticker\\|资金费率' | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":410,"output":1535,"cacheRead":59392,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":61337,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779837402485}}
