{"type":"message","id":"ec1d9fac","parentId":"31ebb99f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T00:10:46.198Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user has two concerns:\n1. They want me to list specific files to push\n2. They're worried about not backing up .openclaw code - if something breaks and they can't revert\n3. They mention the repo is private, so sensitive files are less of a concern (but still need caution)\n\nSince the repo is private, API keys in config files are less risky, but still not ideal to store in git. Let me think about a good approach:\n\n1. The core code that matters is in workspace/scripts/\n2. The .openclaw config files (config.yaml, openclaw.json, crypto/.env) contain API keys\n3. For a private repo, the risk is lower but still present\n\nA good approach: \n- Upload everything except the most sensitive files (API keys)\n- Or: upload a template/redacted version of configs\n- Or: use .gitignore to exclude just the specific sensitive lines/files\n\nLet me check what's actually in the sensitive files and list a comprehensive plan.\n\nLet me also look at the current .gitignore to see what's already excluded.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_xPhfVBh9eQAIAoRUvRFT3708","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat /root/.openclaw/.gitignore 2>/dev/null"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_5E8u10Wtp4mLnrZvyFl39136","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"find /root/.openclaw -maxdepth 2 -type f -not -path '*/.git/*' -not -path '*/node_modules/*' -not -path '*/logs/*' -not -path '*/__pycache__/*' -not -path '*/archive/*' -not -name '*.sqlite*' -not -name '*.pyc' -not -name '*.log' | sort"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":1900,"output":640,"cacheRead":108672,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":111212,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779840638898}}
