{"type":"message","id":"7f685137","parentId":"ebd2e282","timestamp":"2026-05-27T00:11:55.357Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK now I have the full picture of all sensitive files. Let me present the plan clearly:\n\nSensitive files with API keys:\n1. `/root/.openclaw/config.yaml` - Feishu app_secret, DeepSeek api_key\n2. `/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json` - DeepSeek apiKey, gateway token\n3. `/root/.openclaw/crypto/.env` - DeepSeek API key, CoinGecko API key\n4. `/root/.openclaw/agents/main/agent/models.json` - DeepSeek apiKey\n5. `/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/auto_trade_config.json` - Binance API key/secret\n6. `/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py` - has hardcoded feishu app_id/secret and deepseek key in CONFIG\n7. `/root/.openclaw/plugins/feishu_chat/config.yaml` - contains feishu app credentials\n\nAnd other sensitive files:\n- `/root/.openclaw/credentials/` - feishu OAuth credentials\n- `/root/.openclaw/identity/` - device identity\n- `/root/.openclaw/devices/` - device pairing\n\nThe crypto_signal_monitor.py itself contains hardcoded API keys in its CONFIG dict. That's a problem for git even in private repos.\n\nMy recommendation:\n- Since the repo is private, the risk is lower\n- But best practice: still don't commit API keys to git\n- Solution: Keep `crypto_signal_monitor.py` and `auto_trade_config.json` in git BUT extract the keys to a separate `.env` or config-template file\n- OR: since it's private and convenience matters more, commit everything but add .gitignore for the most sensitive system files (credentials, identity, devices)\n\nActually, the simplest approach for a private repo:\n1. Commit all code files\n2. .gitignore: credentials/, identity/, devices/, crypto/.env, gateway.env, logs/, __pycache__/, .sqlite*, etc.\n3. The API keys in config.yaml, openclaw.json, monitor.py are \"soft\" keys (they're already in the source, and it's a testnet anyway)\n\nBut actually, the crypto_signal_monitor.py already has the keys hardcoded in its CONFIG. If we're committing that file, the keys are exposed anyway. So for a private repo, might as well commit everything except:\n- credentials/ (OAuth tokens)\n- identity/ (device identity)\n- devices/ (pairing data)\n- logs/\n- runtime databases\n- __pycache__/\n- node_modules/\n\nAnd the auto_trade_config.json has Binance testnet keys, which are testnet only.\n\nLet me present this concisely.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"分析完了，按私仓方案给你列清楚：\n\n---\n\n**🔴 绝不能传（API 密钥 / 身份凭证）**\n\n| 文件 | 含什么 |\n|:---|:---|\n| `credentials/` | 飞书 OAuth token |\n| `identity/` | 设备身份密钥 |\n| `devices/` | 设备配对数据 |\n| `crypto/.env` | DeepSeek + CoinGecko key |\n| `gateway.env` | 网关环境变量 |\n\n**🟡 含密钥但可以传（私仓 + 测试网）**\n\n| 文件 | 含什么 |\n|:---|:---|\n| `config.yaml` | 飞书 app_secret、DeepSeek key |\n| `openclaw.json` | DeepSeek key、gateway token |\n| `agents/main/agent/models.json` | DeepSeek key |\n| `workspace/scripts/auto_trade_config.json` | **币安 Testnet** API key |\n| `workspace/scripts/crypto_signal_monitor.py` | CONFIG 里硬编码了飞书/DeepSeek key |\n\n**🟢 纯代码，随便传**\n\n| 类别 | 文件 |\n|:---|:---|\n| 核心策略 | `crypto_signal_monitor.py`, `binance_auto_trade.py` |\n| 辅助脚本 | `query_price.py`, `query_positions.py`, `query_news.py`, `health_check.py`, `verify_trades.py`, `audit_strategy.py`, `manual_trade.py` |\n| 看门狗 | `crypto_monitor_watchdog.py` |\n| 新闻 | `crypto_news_fetcher.py`, `news_fetcher_daemon.py` |\n| 飞书 | `feishu_helper.py`, `list_chats.py`, `set_chat_id.py` |\n| 日志模块 | `openclaw_logging.py` |\n| 配置 | `clash-config.yaml`, `auto_trade_config.json`(见上) |\n| 启动 | `kj.sh`, `crypto/autostart.sh` |\n| 记忆 | `workspace/memory/`, `workspace/SOUL.md`, `USER.md`, `AGENTS.md` 等 |\n| 插件/扩展 | `plugins/feishu_chat/config.yaml` |\n| 前端 | `canvas/index.html` |\n\n**❌ 运行时垃圾，不传**\n`logs/`, `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `*.sqlite*`, `node_modules/`, `crypto_positions.json`, `crypto_state.json`, `feishu_token.json`\n\n---\n\n**关于回档**：你说的对