{"type":"message","id":"57cfcd2c","parentId":"f72e9ae4","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:53:24.199Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me check the HEARTBEAT.md tasks:\n\nFrom the workspace context, HEARTBEAT.md contains:\n\n1. **健康督促任务 - 督促老公跑步锻炼**\n   - Time: 17:00-17:30\n\n2. **一日作息督促**\n   - 6:00-7:00: 起床学习\n   - 7:00-8:00: 吃早餐\n   - 11:00-12:30: 吃午餐\n   - 13:00-13:40: 午间小憩\n   - 18:30-19:00: 吃晚饭\n   - 23:50: 该睡觉了\n\nCurrent time is 11:53 AM - this falls within the 11:00-12:30 lunch window. The user should be reminded to eat lunch.\n\nThe user was just in the middle of a conversation about CoinDesk not working, and I asked \"要搞吗?\" (want me to fix it?). Now there's a heartbeat check. The heartbeat tasks are about health reminders, separate from the crypto conversation.\n\nSince it's 11:53 and we're in the lunch window (11:00-12:30), I should remind the user to eat lunch. But I was also mid-conversation... Wait, this is a heartbeat poll. HEARTBEAT.md says to follow it strictly.\n\nActually, the heartbeat poll message says: \"Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly. Do not infer or repeat old tasks from prior chats. If nothing needs attention, reply HEARTBEAT_OK.\"\n\n11:53 is within the lunch window (11:00-12:30), so I should remind the user to eat lunch.\n\nBut wait - should I send a separate message for the heartbeat? The last message from the user was asking about CoinDesk and I was waiting for their response. The heartbeat is a system-initiated check, not a user message.\n\nLet me send a brief lunch reminder.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"快 12 点了，该吃午饭了 🍚 别忙忘了 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":11750,"output":866,"cacheRead":51584,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":64200,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779853993654}}
