{"type":"message","id":"9872a750","parentId":"852afe3f","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:02:52.180Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if it'll be too complicated. Let me think about the simplest approach.\n\nActually, the simplest fix is to just add a few new nodes from the subscription to the existing config. We don't need to rebuild the entire config with proxy-providers - just add USA/Germany nodes that can access CoinGecko.\n\nBut even simpler: since CoinDesk is the current news source but was using HTTP (not HTTPS), and the subscription gives us many more nodes, the minimal change would be to just update the clash-config.yaml with some of the subscription nodes, and then add a rule to route CoinDesk/CoinGecko through those nodes.\n\nActually, the absolute simplest approach: just add a rule in clash-config.yaml that routes `coindesk.com` and `coingecko.com` through the `JP-Tokyo-01` node (which the user confirmed works on their client). No need for proxy-providers or any big refactor.\n\nLet me look at the current clash-config.yaml structure to figure out how to add this routing rule.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"不麻烦，最简单的做法——你客户端日本节点能通，就给 Clash 加两条路由规则，让 CoinDesk/CoinGecko 走日本节点，不动现有其他配置。改一个文件加几行就行 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":295,"output":486,"cacheRead":80640,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":81421,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779854564496}}
