{"type":"message","id":"45c48e82","parentId":"c8e6851c","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:04:05.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the log says \"Start initial Compatible provider CRYPTO-NEWS\" which suggests Clash is treating it as a provider. But wait - I configured it as a proxy-group under `proxy-groups:`, not as a `proxy-providers:`. The message \"Compatible provider\" is interesting.\n\nLet me check if the issue is something else. The coingecko request didn't show up in the TCP connection log. Let me check if maybe the request is still going through the old PROXY group or something.\n\nLet me also try testing CoinGecko WITHOUT proxy to confirm baseline, and try a few other things.\n\nActually, wait - maybe the problem is different. Let me check if the CRYPTO-NEWS health check passed and which node is active.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_yzkmfpG28Omav0zrdakg5724","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9090' 2>/dev/null && echo \"---\"; curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9090/proxies' 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor name in ['CRYPTO-NEWS', 'PROXY']:\n    if name in data.get('proxies', {}):\n        p = data['proxies'][name]\n        print(f\\\"{name}: type={p.get('type')} now={p.get('now')}\\\")\n\" 2>&1","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":118,"output":520,"cacheRead":84736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":85374,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854637493}}
{"type":"message","id":"11b3dca6","parentId":"45c48e82","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:04:06.226Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_yzkmfpG28Omav0zrdakg5724","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"hello\":\"mihomo\"}\n---\nCRYPTO-NEWS: type=Fallback now=HK-Home-03\nPROXY: type=Fallback now=HK-Home-03"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":585,"aggregated":"{\"hello\":\"mihomo\"}\n---\nCRYPTO-NEWS: type=Fallback now=HK-Home-03\nPROXY: type=Fallback now=HK-Home-03","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779854646219}}
{"type":"message","id":"996c35fd","parentId":"11b3dca6","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:04:22.360Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both PROXY and CRYPTO-NEWS are using HK-Home-03 as the active node! That means the health check on JP-Tokyo-01 probably failed (the URL `http://www.gstatic.com/generate_204` might be blocked from China for the JP nodes too), so it fell back to HK-Home-03, which we already know can't access CoinGecko.\n\nThe issue is: the health check URL `http://www.gstatic.com/generate_204` is accessible from HK but not from JP (or the JP nodes fail the check for other reasons).\n\nI need a different approach. Options:\n1. Remove the fallback health check and use a `select` group (manual switching)\n2. Use a different health check URL that works from all nodes\n3. Use `url-test` instead of `fallback`\n\nActually, the health check goes through the proxy itself, so if the proxy node can reach gstatic.com, it should pass. The fact that JP-Tokyo-01 is not being selected as active means the fallback group failed all health checks for JP nodes and moved to HK.\n\nWait, but the user said they're using Japan nodes from their client and it works fine. Maybe there's a difference in how the proxy routes the health check vs actual traffic.\n\nLet me try a different approach: instead of `fallback`, use `url-test` which selects the fastest responding node. Or better yet, try a `load-balance` or just `select` group.\n\nActually, let me try removing the gstatic health check and use `http://cp.cloudflare.com/` or just a simple connectivity test. Or better yet, let me change the approach:\n\nMake CRYPTO-NEWS a simple chain group that tries JP-Tokyo first, then falls back. Or use `relay` or a different strategy.\n\nActually, the simplest fix: since the fallback group uses health checks and the JP nodes fail them, let me change the CRYPTO-NEWS group to use `url-test` instead of `fallback`, and set a more tolerant timeout. URL-test doesn't fall through on failure - it just picks the fastest success.\n\nOr even simpler: just use a `select` group pointing directly to JP-Tokyo-01. But then there's no automatic failover.\n\nLet me try a different URL for health check - maybe `http://www.gstatic.com/generate_204` is blocked.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"JP 节点被 Clash 健康检查判为不通过（`gstatic.com` 可能从 JP 访问有问题），所以回退到了 HK。换成更宽容的 URL 检查："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Z06Exxln1oOItwFPmGTr8759","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/clash-config.yaml","old_string":"  - name: CRYPTO-NEWS\n    type: fallback\n    proxies:\n      - JP-Tokyo-01\n      - JP-Tokyo-02\n      - SG-02\n      - HK-Home-03\n    url: http://www.gstatic.com/generate_204\n    interval: 60\n    timeout: 5","new_string":"  - name: CRYPTO-NEWS\n    type: fallback\n    proxies:\n      - JP-Tokyo-01\n      - JP-Tokyo-02\n      - SG-02\n      - KR-Home-01\n    url: https://www.google.com/generate_204\n    interval: 60\n    timeout: 8"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":146,"output":1304,"cacheRead":85120,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86570,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854646237}}
