{"type":"message","id":"c0685559","parentId":"9d105566","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:04:29.167Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, I also removed HK-Home-03 from CRYPTO-NEWS since we know it doesn't work for CoinGecko. Let me also think about whether using google.com for health check is a good idea - the JP nodes should be able to reach google.com.\n\nActually, let me try a completely different approach. The health check URL probably doesn't matter much. The real issue is that maybe JP nodes just can't be reached from our server. Let me check if the JP server (rb.kunlun01.com:18000) is even reachable.\n\nOr maybe I should just try using `url-test` which picks the fastest responsive node, with a longer timeout.\n\nActually, let me just restart and test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_UJrOtb6vWniFBo1jzuYf0196","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"pkill mihomo && sleep 1 && nohup /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/mihomo -d /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts -f /root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/clash-config.yaml > /root/.openclaw/logs/clash/clash.log 2>&1 & sleep 3 && curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:9090/proxies' | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\ndata = json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor name in ['CRYPTO-NEWS', 'PROXY']:\n    p = data['proxies'].get(name, {})\n    print(f'{name}: now={p.get(\\\"now\\\",\\\"?\\\")}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":8}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":75,"output":530,"cacheRead":86016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":86621,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854662468}}
