-:--:--  0:00:04 --:--:--     0* Connection timed out after 5003 milliseconds\n\r  0     0    0     0    0     0      0      0 --:--:--  0:00:05 --:--:--     0\n* closing connection #0\ncurl: (28) Connection timed out after 5003 milliseconds","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779854714054}}
{"type":"message","id":"6689daf2","parentId":"cdd45771","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:05:21.078Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! DNS resolves to `103.97.3.19` (different from what we got earlier with nslookup). The connection is timing out. The request doesn't show up in Clash log, which is strange.\n\nWait - the `* Uses proxy env variable no_proxy == '*'` line is suspicious. That suggests curl might be using an environment variable for proxy, not the command-line argument. Let me check if there's a `no_proxy` set that blocks the proxy.\n\nActually, `no_proxy == '*'` means the curl command itself is recognizing the proxy but the `no_proxy` environment variable is set to `*` which would skip proxy for everything. But we're using `--proxy` flag which should override.\n\nLet me try with explicit proxy and without the env variable getting in the way:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_fAGcAMmNSAUFfxLHDhkJ3676","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"no_proxy=\"\" curl -v --noproxy '' --proxy http://127.0.0.1:7890 --max-time 5 'https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/ping' 2>&1 | head -15","timeout":8}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":381,"output":454,"cacheRead":87808,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":88643,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854714086}}
{"type":"message","id":"a15dac39","parentId":"6689daf2","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:05:22.413Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_fAGcAMmNSAUFfxLHDhkJ3676","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"% Total    % Received % Xferd  Average Speed   Time    Time     Time  Current\n                                 Dload  Upload   Total   Spent    Left  Speed\n\r  0     0    0     0    0     0      0      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:--     0*   Trying 127.0.0.1:7890...\n* CONNECT tunnel: HTTP/1.1 negotiated\n* allocate connect buffer\n* Establish HTTP proxy tunnel to api.coingecko.com:443\n> CONNECT api.coingecko.com:443 HTTP/1.1\r\n> Host: api.coingecko.com:443\r\n> User-Agent: curl/8.14.1\r\n> Proxy-Connection: Keep-Alive\r\n> \r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 Connection established\r\n< \r\n* CONNECT phase completed\n* CONNECT tunnel established, response 200"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":1213,"aggregated":"% Total    % Received % Xferd  Average Speed   Time    Time     Time  Current\n                                 Dload  Upload   Total   Spent    Left  Speed\n\r  0     0    0     0    0     0      0      0 --:--:-- --:--:-- --:--:--     0*   Trying 127.0.0.1:7890...\n* CONNECT tunnel: HTTP/1.1 negotiated\n* allocate connect buffer\n* Establish HTTP proxy tunnel to api.coingecko.com:443\n> CONNECT api.coingecko.com:443 HTTP/1.1\r\n> Host: api.coingecko.com:443\r\n> User-Agent: curl/8.14.1\r\n> Proxy-Connection: Keep-Alive\r\n> \r\n< HTTP/1.1 200 Connection established\r\n< \r\n* CONNECT phase completed\n* CONNECT tunnel established, response 200","cwd":"/root/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779854722388}}
{"type":"message","id":"684ce7f6","parentId":"a15dac39","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:05:30.799Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now the request goes through the proxy! And we get a `200 Connection established` from the Clash proxy. Let me see the full response.\n\nBut wait - earlier requests also seemed to try the proxy but timed out. Let me look at the previous verbose output again:\n\n```\n* Uses proxy env variable no_proxy == '*'\n* Host api.coingecko.com:443 was resolved.\n* IPv6: 2001::9df0:23\n* IPv4: 103.97.3.19\n*   Trying [2001::9df0:23]:443...\n*   Trying 103.97.3.19:443...\n```\n\nThis was trying to connect directly to the IP addresses, NOT through the proxy. The `no_proxy` environment issue caused curl to skip the proxy.\n\nAnd now with `no_proxy=\"\"` and `--noproxy ''`, it properly goes through the proxy: `* Trying 127.0.0.1:7890...` → `CONNECT tunnel established`.\n\nSo the issue all along was the `no_proxy` environment variable that was blocking proxy for some requests! Let me now test if CoinGecko actually works through the proxy now.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"环境变量问题！`no_proxy=*` 导致部分请求跳过了代理。现在正确走了 Clash："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_geESO91dMpRt8G6xS2tI2049","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"no_proxy=\"\" curl -s --noproxy '' --proxy http://127.0.0.1:7890 -w '\\nhttp_code=%{http_code} time=%{time_total}s' --max-time 10 'https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/ping' 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":240,"output":656,"cacheRead":88448,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":89344,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854722441}}
