{"type":"message","id":"5ab24ffe","parentId":"cb61a944","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:05:39.425Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CoinGecko works now! It returns `{\"gecko_says\":\"(V3) To the Moon!\"}` with HTTP 200 and 0.8 second response time.\n\nSo the fix is working:\n1. CRYPTO-NEWS proxy group using JP-Tokyo-01 active node\n2. CoinGecko is reachable through it\n\nNow the issue is that the Python scripts use the `requests` library which respects the `http_proxy`/`https_proxy` environment variables, and the `no_proxy` issue might affect them too. Let me check if the scripts explicitly set the proxy or rely on environment variables.\n\nActually, looking at the `auto_trade_config.json`, the proxy is explicitly passed in the `proxies` parameter of `requests.get/post()`, so the Python scripts shouldn't be affected by the `no_proxy` env variable.\n\nBut let me also check the `crypto_news_fetcher.py` to see how it makes requests.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"CoinGecko 通了！ `\"To the Moon!\"` ✅\n\n核心问题是环境变量 `no_proxy=*` 让 curl 跳过了代理，但 Python 脚本用的是 `requests` 直接传 `proxies` 参数，不受影响。现在 CoinDesk 也测试一下："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_pFd4YQij7szEJUDL08BW2603","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"no_proxy=\"\" curl -s --noproxy '' --proxy http://127.0.0.1:7890 -w '\\nhttp_code=%{http_code} time=%{time_total}s' --max-time 10 'https://www.coindesk.com/arc/outboundfeeds/rss/' 2>&1 | head -3","timeout":15}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":43,"output":612,"cacheRead":89088,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":89743,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779854731861}}
