{"type":"message","id":"ce26c8bb","parentId":"aed6e180","timestamp":"2026-05-27T04:48:57.109Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"CRYPTO-NEWS is now on KR-Home-01 (Korean node). The JP-Tokyo-01 must have failed health check and it fell back. The SSL error with CoinGecko news might be related to the KR node.\n\nLet me fix the CRYPTO-NEWS group to be more stable. The issue might be that the fallback with health checks keeps cycling through nodes and some are unstable. Let me try a different approach - change to `url-test` which picks the fastest responding node, or increase timeout. Or I could just add more robust nodes from the subscription.\n\nActually, let me first check if CoinGecko ping still works through the current setup:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_4XW4pgJKAmrXQkTZyz0i7965","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"no_proxy=\"\" curl -s --noproxy '' --proxy http://127.0.0.1:7890 -w '\\nhttp=%{http_code}' --max-time 8 'https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/ping' 2>&1; echo; no_proxy=\"\" curl -s --noproxy '' --proxy http://127.0.0.1:7890 -w '\\nhttp=%{http_code}' --max-time 8 'https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/news' -H 'x-cg-demo-api-key: CG-DZoCE8UMF3FWpeYhBMvqGq4g' 2>&1 | head -c 200","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":247,"output":498,"cacheRead":97536,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98281,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779857329243}}
