{"type":"message","id":"5ba48143","parentId":"663b6003","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:25:22.668Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I don't see any heartbeat configuration in openclaw.json. Let me check the docs for heartbeat scheduling. The heartbeat system might be a built-in feature with a fixed interval that can't be easily changed, or it might need to be configured differently.\n\nActually, looking at the prompt, the heartbeat message content describes:\n```\n## Heartbeats\nHeartbeat prompt: Read HEARTBEAT.md if it exists (workspace context). Follow it strictly...\n```\n\nThis suggests the system periodically sends a heartbeat prompt. The interval might be fixed at something like 1 hour or 30 minutes.\n\nThe issue the user is facing: the HEARTBEAT.md has time-window tasks, but the heartbeat interval might be too infrequent to catch narrow windows like 13:00-13:40 (40 minutes for nap).\n\nLooking at the conversation, I did catch the lunch window (11:00-12:30 is 90 minutes) at 11:53. But the nap window (40 minutes) was missed.\n\nThe best fix would be to use OpenClaw cron jobs for time-critical tasks instead of relying on heartbeat timing. Or I can suggest adjusting the HEARTBEAT.md tasks to have wider windows.\n\nLet me also check - can I see when the last heartbeat was triggered?","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Jq0LXF3PikNW0bB0QOYr4036","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r 'heartbeat\\|HEARTBEAT' /root/.openclaw/logs/ 2>/dev/null | tail -5; echo \"===\"; journalctl -u openclaw --no-pager -n 20 2>/dev/null | grep -i 'heart' | tail -3"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":672,"output":634,"cacheRead":107904,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":109210,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779863113638}}
