{"type":"message","id":"6bcb8756","parentId":"c7f9d866","timestamp":"2026-05-27T06:37:15.533Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The test cron at 14:35 didn't fire. The gateway didn't hot-reload the cron config. Also the nohup restart didn't actually restart the gateway (PID 13975 unchanged).\n\nI need a different approach to reload the cron config. Let me check:\n\n1. Can I use the OpenClaw API to reload? The gateway has a control API on port 18789.\n2. Can I kill the gateway process and start a new one?\n\nActually, the problem might be simpler. The OpenClaw cron system might need the gateway to be restarted in a specific way. Since the nohup restart didn't work (the PID didn't change), maybe it failed silently.\n\nLet me try a different approach - use the OpenClaw CLI with the internal API, or kill and restart the process manually.\n\nWait, actually, let me check if the cron system is even enabled/configured in OpenClaw. Maybe the cron feature needs to be explicitly enabled.\n\nLet me check the OpenClaw docs for cron configuration.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"没触发，gateway 没有热重载 cron。让我换个方式："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_P1IBqCvyp9gYK5nwflMe4716","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"grep -r 'cron\\|schedule' /root/.openclaw/openclaw.json 2>/dev/null; echo \"===\"; curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:18789/api/cron/jobs' -H 'Authorization: Bearer e4755a063458c0e582ed04a7fcc9b5b13ea25a37bef0601b' 2>&1 | head -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":321,"output":601,"cacheRead":54016,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":54938,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779863826841}}
