{"type":"message","id":"8a88ce39","parentId":"24ecf13a","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:32:08.204Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if they need to restart the gateway every time they switch models. Let me think about this.\n\nThe gateway needs to restart to pick up config changes, but once both models are loaded in the config, switching between them shouldn't require a restart. The `/model` command should work without restarting the gateway.\n\nHowever, the current model list needs to be loaded at startup. So after this first restart, both v4-pro and v4-flash will be available, and switching between them with `/model` should work without restart.\n\nBut we haven't restarted yet! So the current running gateway only knows about v4-pro. After the next restart, both models will be available and switching will be instant.\n\nLet me clarify this.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"第一次加模型需要重启一次让 gateway 加载列表。之后两个都在了，`/model deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` / `/model deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` 随时秒切，不用重启 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":353,"output":356,"cacheRead":96256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":96965,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779895921904}}
{"type":"message","id":"570f1323","parentId":"8a88ce39","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:33:05.375Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e44a5c4f4a8b37a12458ad21ed\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"sender\": \"用户124241\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 23:33 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"用户124241 (ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"name\": \"用户124241\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e44a5c4f4a8b37a12458ad21ed]\n用户124241: 我在想能不能聊天的时候用flash代码修改的时候用pro"}],"timestamp":1779895985329}}
{"type":"message","id":"5e468107","parentId":"570f1323","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:33:30.832Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants a smart model routing:\n- Chat/conversation → flash (cheaper/faster)\n- Code modifications → pro (better at coding)\n\nThis is an interesting architecture question. With the current OpenClaw setup, this could be done in a few ways:\n\n1. **Session-level model switch** - use `/model` command to switch. But manual.\n2. **Agent-level routing** - separate agents for chat vs coding. But complex.\n3. **Custom routing in the intent router** - the Python feishu_intent_router.py could route different intents to different sessions with different models.\n\nLooking at the current architecture:\n- `crypto_signal_monitor.py` already uses DeepSeek v4-pro directly via API (not through OpenClaw LLM)\n- The `feishu_intent_router.py` routes some messages to Python scripts (bypassing LLM)\n- Messages that reach LLM (me) are handled by the configured default model\n\nThe cleanest approach would be to modify the intent router to:\n- Code/modify/script related keywords → route to a session using v4-pro\n- Chat/casual conversation → route to a session using v4-flash\n\nBut that's complex. Simpler options:\n1. Set up a separate sub-agent for coding tasks with pro model\n2. Use OpenClaw's agent system to have \"chat agent\" (flash) vs \"coding agent\" (pro)\n\nActually, I think the most practical approach is to:\n1. Set flash as the default model (for chat)\n2. For coding tasks, use `/model deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro` then do the work\n\nOr better yet, we could modify the feishu_intent_router.py to create a two-agent setup. Let me think about this...\n\nActually, OpenClaw supports per-agent model configuration. We could set up:\n- Main agent: flash (for chat)\n- Code agent: pro (spawned for coding tasks)\n\nOr we could use the sessions system.\n\nBut the simplest approach might be to just use `/model` or to set up a custom command. Let me suggest a practical approach.\n\nActually, the most feasible approach given the architecture: I can detect coding intent myself and respond accordingly. When the user asks me to modify files or diagnose issues, I'm already the LLM. The issue is I'm running under whatever model is configured.\n\nThe best approach for this: set up the feishu_intent_router to detect code-related intents and route them to a separate session/agent with pro model. The rest goes to flash.\n\nBut wait - looking at AGENTS.md, the intent router already handles crypto keywords (price, positions, etc) and routes them to scripts. Maybe we can add code/modify/script keywords to the router too.\n\nActually, I think the simplest and most maintainable approach is:\n1. Make flash the default in config.yaml\n2. Use OpenClaw's session-level model override for coding sessions\n\nOr even simpler: I can use the `/model` command to switch when needed. But that's manual.\n\nLet me suggest a plan: set up the intent router to detect coding keywords and spawn a sub-agent with pro model, while the main chat agent uses flash.\n\nActually wait - I think the solution is simpler. We can keep the main config with pro as default, but I (the agent) can switch to flash for chat-heavy conversations using session model override. But the user wants automatic routing.\n\nThe most practical plan: \n1. Set flash as main default for responsiveness/cheapness\n2. Create a \"coding\" session template with pro model\n3. The intent router detects code keywords → spawns coding session (pro)\n4. Everything else → main session (flash)\n\nLet me present this plan to the user.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"可以的，思路是：\n\n| 你说的话 | 走什么模型 |\n|:---|:---|\n| 闲聊、查询、日常 | flash（快 + 便宜） |\n| 改代码、修 bug、重写脚本 | pro（质量高） |\n\n实现方案：改 `feishu_intent_router.py`，加一层模型路由：\n- 检测到「改 / 写 / 修复 / 脚本 / 代码」关键词 → 触发一个 pro 模型会话\n- 其余 → 默认走 flash\n\n或者更简单：把默认切 flash，我收到编程任务时 spawn 一个 pro 子会话，用 `/model` 切完干活。\n\n要做吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":443,"output":1735,"cacheRead":96512,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98690,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779895985356}}
{"type":"message","id":"fa36c0d8","parentId":"5e468107","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:35:22.857Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e44bd6f34a0b3b679dc6b8ff93\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"sender\": \"用户124241\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 23:35 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"用户124241 (ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"name\": \"用户124241\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e44bd6f34a0b3b679dc6b8ff93]\n用户124241: 哪个好一点,ai分析那里就还是继续用pro不用管"}],"timestamp":1779896122812}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8b6f759","parentId":"fa36c0d8","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:35:33.687Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking which approach is better. They want:\n1. AI analysis (monitor's DeepSeek calls for signal evaluation) to keep using pro\n2. For our chat, they want flash for chatting, pro for code modifications\n\nLet me think about the two approaches:\n\nOption A: Modify feishu_intent_router.py\n- Detect keywords in messages\n- Route to different model sessions\n- More complex, requires router modification\n- Need gateway restart\n\nOption B: Default flash, spawn pro for code tasks\n- Simpler to implement\n- Default model is flash for everyday chat\n- I spawn sub-sessions with pro for code work\n- More natural - I decide when to use pro\n\nOption B is simpler and more flexible. I can use `sessions_spawn` with `model: \"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash\"` for code work.\n\nWait, actually, the simplest approach: in config.yaml, set default to flash. Then when I need to do code work, I switch to pro using `/model`. But that means the whole session switches.\n\nActually, the cleanest approach: spawn sub-agents with pro model for code tasks. I keep the main conversation on flash.\n\nLet me recommend Option B - it's simpler and doesn't require modifying the intent router.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"第二个更好——不碰路由器，只改默认模型 + spawn 子会话。\n\n**方案：**\n1. `config.yaml` 默认切 flash\n2. 你要改代码时，我 spawn 一个 pro 子会话干活，干完结果推回来\n3. AI 分析那边不受影响（monitor 里写死了 pro）\n\n**好处：**\n- 不需要改路由器，不引入新 bug\n- 只改一行默认模型\n- 子会话隔离，pro 干代码不怕污染聊天上下文\n\n要我改吗？"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":504,"output":656,"cacheRead":96896,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98056,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779896122851}}
{"type":"message","id":"c2f06a2c","parentId":"d8b6f759","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:37:44.286Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6e44b29428b0b11657dd55be2f0\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"conversation_label\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"sender\": \"用户124241\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Wed 2026-05-27 23:37 GMT+8\",\n  \"group_subject\": \"oc_a04a61675c784d76c345fde6501e8f49\",\n  \"is_group_chat\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"用户124241 (ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166)\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_6d6f52f26015356263395c9b4abfd166\",\n  \"name\": \"用户124241\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6e44b29428b0b11657dd55be2f0]\n用户124241: 可以,但是推回来会不会左右脑互搏"}],"timestamp":1779896264220}}
{"type":"message","id":"5e47f75c","parentId":"c2f06a2c","timestamp":"2026-05-27T15:37:56.578Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is concerned about the \"left brain right brain\" problem - where spawning a sub-agent for code work might cause confusion or inconsistency. \n\nThe concern is valid: if I spawn a pro sub-agent, how does it communicate back? The sub-agent would work independently and then return results. But the main agent (me) would still need to relay those results. The user might see two different \"personas\" or the handoff might be awkward.\n\nLet me think about this... Actually, for code changes, the workflow would be:\n1. User asks for a code change\n2. I (flash model) receive it\n3. I spawn a pro sub-agent to do the actual coding\n4. The sub-agent completes and returns the result\n5. I present the result to the user\n\nThe user wouldn't see the sub-agent directly - they'd only see me. So no \"left-right brain\" confusion from the user's perspective.\n\nBut the user might be worried about the sub-agent doing something wrong and me not catching it. Or about the sub-agent polluting the context of the main session.\n\nActually, the real question is simpler: should I just use `sessions_spawn` for code work, or should I use a different approach like `sessions_send` to an existing pro session?\n\nLet me explain that the sub-agent is transparent to the user - they only see me, and the sub-agent is like me \"putting on glasses\" to focus on code. No brain split visible.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"不会。子会话是后台干活，你看不到它——你看到的始终只有我。\n\n具体流程：\n1. 你说「改 X 脚本」\n2. 我 spawn 一个 pro 子会话，把任务丢给它，它闷头写代码\n3. 写完结果返回给我，我检查没问题再告诉你「改好了」\n4. 你全程只跟我对话，子会话就像我脑子里的后台线程\n\n你的体验不变，只是改代码的时候我「戴上眼镜」用心一点 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":524,"output":725,"cacheRead":97280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98529,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead