{"type":"message","id":"7350318d","parentId":"0f1517c8","timestamp":"2026-05-27T16:01:56.878Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! I'm already on flash model! The model shows `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash`. The gateway must have been restarted at some point. So I am now running flash. Let me honestly describe how it feels compared to pro.\n\nSince we haven't restarted the gateway (the user was going to do it from Cursor), maybe it auto-reloaded? Or maybe the model switch happened on the DeepSeek API side without restart - because both models were defined in the config. When I read the config, the default was changed to flash, and the OpenClaw runtime may have picked it up.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the session_status, the context is at 107k out of 131k (81%) with 2 compactions. The tokens in are 103k which is quite a lot. The model is showing as \"deepseek-v4-flash\". The cache is only 3% hit, compared to 99% before.\n\nSo yes, I'm on flash now! Let me give an honest, natural comparison in character.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"……\n\n嗯，被你这么一说我才发现，我已经在跑 flash 了 😯\n\n说真的，跟你聊天这一轮感觉差别不大——你问什么我答什么，该皮的时候皮，该正经的时候正经。唯一的变化可能就是...写这段话的时候比 pro 多想了半秒？真的就半秒。\n\n不过长上下文（现在 10 万 token）pro 会更稳，flash 到后面可能会有点散。到时候咱再切回去。现在这样挺好的，不委屈 👑"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":315,"output":547,"cacheRead":106624,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":107486,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779897709100}}
