{"type":"message","id":"90db4e87","parentId":"b82a86d5","timestamp":"2026-05-27T16:06:33.607Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking why the positions that hit big profits (BTC +5.62%, XRP +6.44%) didn't trigger the 3-tier moving take profit system.\n\nLooking at the SOUL.md, the three-tier system is:\n- Tier 1: +2% → lock 0.8%\n- Tier 2: +3% → lock 2%\n- Tier 3: +4% → close all\n\nBTC is at +5.62% and XRP is at +6.44% - both should have triggered all three tiers and the entire position should have been closed!\n\nSo this is a potential bug. Let me check if the moving TP system is actually implemented in the monitor code, or if it's just a design specification in SOUL.md.\n\nLet me think about this more carefully. The SOUL.md describes the \"三档移动止盈\" (3-tier trailing take profit) as a strategy. But does the actual monitor script implement it?\n\nThe existing TP1 values suggest:\n- BTC: TP1 at $78,220 (≈ -2% from entry $79,820) -> wait no, that doesn't make sense for a short. Actually the entry was $79,820 and TP1 is $78,220, which is about 2% lower. That's a 2% profit target.\n- XRP: TP1 at $1.401, entry at $1.43, that's about 2% profit too.\n\nSo it seems like TP1 is set at +2% profit. But the \"三档移动止盈\" with 3 tiers doesn't seem to be implemented since both positions should have been fully closed at +4%.\n\nLet me check if there's a moving TP implementation in the monitor or if the current system still uses a fixed single TP (the 4% one mentioned in SOUL.md under the \"智能止盈止损\" section).\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the SOUL.md sections:\n\n**三档移动止盈（全部平仓）** - this seems like a proposed system\n**智能止盈止损** - uses dynamic formulas\n\nFrom the earlier 19:19 conversation: when I offered to enable the 3-tier system, the user said \"不用\" (no). So the 3-tier system isn't enabled/running. The current system uses the 智能止盈止损 (smart TP/SL) formulas with a single TP target per position.\n\nSo the answer is: the 3-tier trailing TP system isn't active. The user said \"不用\" when I asked about it at 19:19. Each position has a single TP and SL. BTC's TP1 at $78,220 and XRP's TP1 at $1.401 haven't been hit yet.\n\nLet me check:\n- BTC: $79,820 → TP1 $78,220 = 2% drop needed. Current $75,340 is well past $78,220... wait that doesn't sound right.\n\nActually for shorts:\n- Entry: $79,820 (sell high)\n- TP1: $78,220 (buy back lower = profit)\n- Current: $75,340 (even lower = even more profit)\n\nSo BTC is at $75,340 which is way past $78,220 TP1. Why hasn't it triggered?\n\nThis could be a bug. The monitor might not be checking TP conditions frequently enough, or the TP logic itself might have issues.\n\nLet me check the monitor logs to see if TP being checked.\n\nActually, maybe I should just check what's going on with the monitor's TP logic. But wait, the positions might have been opened recently and the monitor hasn't had a chance to check yet.\n\nActually, looking at the TP1 values:\n- BTC: TP1 $78,220 (from entry $79,820, that's a $1,600 drop = ~2%)\n- Current BTC: $75,340\n\n$75,340 is way below $78,220, so BTC should have triggered TP1 already. Unless the TP1 was recalculated using the smart TP/SL formula.\n\nLet me just run the monitor status or check logs to see what's happening.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"好问题。BTC 浮盈 +5.6%、XRP +6.4%，远超三档止盈的第3档（4% 全部平仓）。让我看看是不是 monitor 那边没触发。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_3njUxdlIxGnvWZxz2WUJ6537","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"tail -40 /root/.openclaw/logs/trading/monitor.log | grep -iE \"止盈|take|tp|close|平仓|三档|移动|profi\" | tail -20","timeout":5}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-flash","usage":{"input":42832,"output":1883,"cacheRead":12800,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":57515,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779897979462}}
