{"type":"message","id":"8774f26d","parentId":"06c53fba","timestamp":"2026-05-27T16:10:03.635Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Still failing with \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected.\" The issue is that for SHORT positions, to close them we need to BUY (not SELL), and the `reduceOnly` flag might be the problem.\n\nWait, actually looking back at the `close_all_positions` code:\n- If amt > 0 (LONG), side = SELL (reduce)\n- If amt < 0 (SHORT), side = BUY (reduce)\n\nBut in my code I used the same logic: `side = 'BUY' if amt > 0 else 'SELL'` for shorts... wait that's wrong! For SHORT positions (negative amount), closing means BUYING back. Let me re-check my code.\n\nLooking at my Python code:\n```python\nside = 'BUY' if amt > 0 else 'SELL'\n```\n\nFor SOL SHORT with amt=-2.38: side = 'SELL' (wants to sell more shorts, not close them!)\n\nActually wait, the `get_all_positions` returns `amount: -2.38` for a short. To close it, we need to BUY (go long) to net to zero. So the side should be BUY for shorts (negative amount).\n\nBut my code has `'BUY' if amt > 0 else 'SELL'` - this is WRONG. When amt < 0 (short), it sets side to SELL, which means selling more - the opposite of what we want.\n\nAnd the `close_all_positions()` in the original code also has:\n```python\nside = 'SELL' if amt > 0 else 'BUY'\n```\nThis is correct: if amt > 0 → SELL, if amt < 0 → BUY.\n\nLet me fix the side logic AND also try without the reduceOnly flag. Maybe the reduceOnly flag is causing issues for some reason.\n\nActually, the error \"ReduceOnly Order is rejected\" means Binance doesn't want the reduceOnly flag. Let me try without it.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"问题是方向和 reduceOnly 都有问题。让我修正："},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_2U3IguEgJJ5bBTKiK2mt8206","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cd ~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts && python3 -c \"\nimport binance_auto_trade as bat\n\npositions = bat.get_all_positions()\nprint(f'平 {len(